body:
Update after retesting on a fresh TPU v6e VM with the same software versions (JAX/jaxlib 0.10.2 and libtpu 0.0.42.1):

The current full producer/consumer composition no longer reproduces the device halt. I added a diagnostic switch that bypasses the canonical-buffer copy and passes the ordinary JAX-built lookup tables directly to the SparseCore consumer. All of the following now execute successfully and match the CPU references:

- SF1: Q4.1, Q4.2, and Q4.3;
- SF5: Q4.1, Q4.2, and Q4.3;
- fused, chunked, and staged SparseCore plans;
- direct JAX-builder output -> SparseCore consumer, without an intermediate canonical copy.

The previously posted standalone synthetic reductions also continue to pass. Therefore I still do not have a failing standalone reproducer, and I will not reopen the issue based on the earlier attribution. The original failure likely depended on an implementation detail in the earlier full composition that is no longer present. I will keep the direct-handoff case as a regression test and follow up only if I can isolate a genuinely failing case.
